From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hobbyquaker <hobbyquaker@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rpi: take the measured EMMC2 clock rate, not its maximum

The firmware answers GET_CLOCK_RATE with the last rate set by
SET_CLOCK_RATE, which U-Boot never sends, so it reads 0 for EMMC2.
Since "arm: rpi: fallback to max clock rate for MMC clock" (0a36afa,
v2023.04) bcm2835_get_mmc_clock() then returns the clock's maximum,
500 MHz on a Pi 4, while EMMC2 really runs at 100 MHz. sdhci takes that
as its base clock and programs the divider for 50 MHz as 500/10, so the
card runs at 10 MHz: SD reads at about 4.8 MB/s instead of 24 MB/s.

For EMMC2 ask for the measured rate before falling back to the maximum,
rounded to whole MHz so that a measurement a little above 100 MHz does not
halve the card clock again. The other clocks keep their behaviour.

Measured on a Pi 4 B (openccu-lite task 381): 16 MiB raw read 3.47 s ->
0.70 s, the 31 MB kernel from ext4 6.5 s -> 1.34 s, the 55 MiB initrd
from FAT 11.9 s -> 2.4 s, as with U-Boot 2023.01.
---
diff -ru a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/include/mach/mbox.h b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/include/mach/mbox.h
--- a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/include/mach/mbox.h
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/include/mach/mbox.h
@@ -224,6 +224,7 @@
 
 #define BCM2835_MBOX_TAG_GET_CLOCK_RATE	0x00030002
 #define BCM2835_MBOX_TAG_GET_MAX_CLOCK_RATE	0x00030004
+#define BCM2835_MBOX_TAG_GET_CLOCK_RATE_MEASURED	0x00030047
 #define BCM2835_MBOX_TAG_GET_MIN_CLOCK_RATE	0x00030007
 
 #define BCM2835_MBOX_CLOCK_ID_EMMC	1
diff -ru a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/msg.c b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/msg.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/msg.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/msg.c
@@ -99,6 +99,26 @@
 
 	clock_rate = msg_clk->get_clock_rate.body.resp.rate_hz;
 
+	/*
+	 * EMMC2 (BCM2711): the firmware reports a current rate only after a
+	 * SET_CLOCK_RATE, which U-Boot never sends, and its maximum (500 MHz)
+	 * is five times the rate the clock really runs at (100 MHz). Taken as
+	 * the base clock, the maximum makes sdhci divide 50 MHz down to 10 MHz.
+	 * Ask for the measured rate first, rounded to whole MHz: a measurement
+	 * a little above 100 MHz would otherwise halve the card clock again.
+	 */
+	if (clock_rate == 0 && clock_id == BCM2835_MBOX_CLOCK_ID_EMMC2) {
+		BCM2835_MBOX_INIT_HDR(msg_clk);
+		BCM2835_MBOX_INIT_TAG(&msg_clk->get_clock_rate,
+				      GET_CLOCK_RATE_MEASURED);
+		msg_clk->get_clock_rate.body.req.clock_id = clock_id;
+
+		ret = bcm2835_mbox_call_prop(BCM2835_MBOX_PROP_CHAN, &msg_clk->hdr);
+		if (!ret)
+			clock_rate = (msg_clk->get_clock_rate.body.resp.rate_hz +
+				      500000) / 1000000 * 1000000;
+	}
+
 	if (clock_rate == 0) {
 		BCM2835_MBOX_INIT_HDR(msg_clk);
 		BCM2835_MBOX_INIT_TAG(&msg_clk->get_clock_rate, GET_MAX_CLOCK_RATE);
-- 
2.43.0
